# ================================================================================
# BINANCE RESEARCH BOT - DEPLOYMENT .ENV GUIDE
# ================================================================================
# This file explains which .env to use for different deployment scenarios
# ================================================================================

# ========== LOCAL DEVELOPMENT ==========
# Use: backend/.env (main config)
# Profiles: Create separate terminal sessions with different BOT_PROFILE_ID

# ========== DOCKER / SINGLE INSTANCE DEPLOYMENT ==========
# Backend runs ONE profile at a time
# Use: backend/.env only
# Set BOT_PROFILE_ID in the main .env
# Example:
#   docker run -e BOT_PROFILE_ID=conservative backend:latest
#   docker run -e BOT_PROFILE_ID=aggressive backend:latest

# ========== VERCEL FRONTEND DEPLOYMENT ==========
# Frontend connects to backend via HTTP (no local .env needed)
# Environment variables needed on Vercel:
#   NEXT_PUBLIC_BACKEND_CONSERVATIVE_URL=https://conservative-backend.example.com
#   NEXT_PUBLIC_BACKEND_AGGRESSIVE_URL=https://aggressive-backend.example.com
# Or use default localhost:5001 and localhost:5002 for local testing

# ========== RECOMMENDED PRODUCTION SETUP ==========
# Option A: Multiple Backend Instances (Recommended)
# - Conservative Profile: runs on separate VPS/Docker with conservative.env
# - Aggressive Profile: runs on separate VPS/Docker with aggressive.env
# - Frontend: Vercel (points to both backend instances)

# Option B: Single Backend with Time-Based Switching
# - One backend process
# - Cron job switches BOT_PROFILE_ID at scheduled times
# - Requires restarting backend service

# ========== FILES TO UPLOAD ==========
# To Vercel (Frontend):
#   - frontend/.env.production (only BACKEND_URLs)
#   - Or use environment variables in Vercel dashboard

# To Backend Hosting:
#   - backend/.env (main config)
#   - backend/profiles/conservative.env OR backend/profiles/aggressive.env
#   - Set BOT_PROFILE_ID=conservative or aggressive

# ========== PROFILE-SPECIFIC OVERRIDES ==========
# Each profile .env file ONLY overrides these sections:
# - Risk management (BOT_RISK_PER_TRADE_PCT, BOT_MAX_*_LOSS_PCT)
# - Trade limits (BOT_MAX_TRADES_PER_DAY, BOT_COOLDOWN_MINUTES)
# - Position management (BOT_PARTIAL_TP_FRACTION, BOT_TRAILING_*)
# - Leverage (BOT_ENABLE_LEVERAGE_2X)
#
# All strategy methods (M1-M6) are enabled in main .env - profiles only change RISK
